c(87, "§3.3 Against these, 119 price-praise reviews concentrated in E1 — 'I'm only paying to support the developers'; 'a one-time charge is a lot less exploitative, and doesn't come with the same guilt'; 'Best $8.99 spent in a long time!'; 27 E1 reviews (mean 4.78) chose Done because of one-time pricing — interpretation: the cap was acceptable when the unlock was a $4–9 one-off read as fair, became the front door to a subscription read as unjustified for a checklist, then was poisoned by fake-urgency offers and purchases that did not apply; do not conclude 'lower the price' — restore a trustworthy one-time or low-commitment path and make it actually work", "product-rule",
  "Against the objections sit 119 price-praise reviews (mean 3.82), concentrated in E1 (63, 6.7% of E1): 'I'm only paying to support the developers'; 'a one-time charge is a lot less exploitative, and doesn't come with the same guilt'; 'Best $8.99 spent in a long time!'; 27 E1 reviews (mean 4.78) say one-time pricing was the reason they chose Done; interpretation: the cap was acceptable when the unlock was a $4–9 one-off reviewers read as fair, became the front door to an annual subscription read as unjustified for a 'checklist', and was then poisoned by fake-urgency offers and purchases that did not apply — do not conclude 'lower the price' alone; restore a trustworthy one-time or low-commitment path, and make it actually work",
  "one-time era vs subscription era", "purchase-driver", "119 (3.82); E1 63 (6.7%); 27 at 4.78", "build-paid", "interpretation", "yes",
  ["1860418284","3441366071","5885951702"])
